#! ia 1.0

@plan marketplace-public-launch
  meaning
    says "Take the public catalogue from its first local cut to a published, host-qualified repository."
  work
    title "Public catalogue launch"
    status open
    source "docs/roadmap.md"

@milestone marketplace-published
  meaning
    says "The catalogue is on GitHub as inventarch/marketplace, installs from Git in Claude Code and Codex, and its gates pass in CI on all three systems."
  work
    title "Published and qualified"
    status open
    plan @plan marketplace-public-launch
    exit "The repository is pushed by the operator, CI passes on main, and the host smoke runs record a pass for Claude Code and Codex at exact versions."
    source "docs/roadmap.md"

@task qualify-claude-code
  meaning
    says "Install ia@inventarch from GitHub in Claude Code at a named version, after removing the CLI-rendered registration, and exercise it with realistic prompts: the three entry points trigger, the session hook prints the bootstrap, the account offer appears once at startup and stays silent when suppressed, the governance probe fires in a governed repository with no governance kit, the IA door starts from .mcp.json and its tools answer as mcp__plugin_ia_ia__*, a compaction re-injects the task pin, a kit's handlers run and a pre block applies only with .ia/governance.json, and agents dispatch with only their allowlisted tools."
  work
    title "Qualify the catalogue in Claude Code"
    status open
    milestone @milestone marketplace-published
    owner "Unassigned"
    start "2026-10-30"
    source "docs/roadmap.md"

@task qualify-codex
  meaning
    says "Run tools/smoke-codex.mjs against a real Codex executable after every manifest, skill or CODEX.md change, and commit its report."
  work
    title "Qualify the catalogue in Codex"
    status open
    milestone @milestone marketplace-published
    owner "Unassigned"
    start "2026-10-30"
    source "docs/roadmap.md"

@task native-qualification-refresh
  meaning
    says "Run the native qualification shards (tools/run-native-tests.mjs) on Ubuntu, Windows and macOS against the 3.4.1 pins and the re-cut kits, and keep the reports."
  work
    title "Refresh native qualification on 3.4.1"
    status open
    milestone @milestone marketplace-published
    owner "Unassigned"
    start "2026-10-30"
    source "docs/roadmap.md"

@task account-offer-key-in-spec
  meaning
    says "Propose to inventarch/ia that the host-plugin-distribution spec name the accountOffer key of ~/.ia/config.json beside updateCheck, so ia doctor reports it; the core already honours it."
  work
    title "Name accountOffer in the IA home spec"
    status proposed
    milestone @milestone marketplace-published
    owner "Unassigned"
    start "2026-10-30"
    source "docs/roadmap.md"

@task bindings-as-records
  meaning
    says "Lower .ia/bindings.json, an interim sidecar, to execution-binding records once the CLI admits them for kit capabilities, so bind and rebind become ia preview and ia author."
  work
    title "Lower bindings to execution-binding records"
    status proposed
    milestone @milestone marketplace-published
    owner "Unassigned"
    start "2026-10-30"
    source "docs/roadmap.md"

@task authoring-method-qualification
  meaning
    says "Qualify the ia-authoring kit's method closure: write config/method-qualification-ia-authoring.json with a reviewed execution contract for every runner in its checks.json (the trigger evaluation needs a reviewed executor profile first), and carry it in tests/carried-method-executors.test.mjs beside ia-kb."
  work
    title "Qualify the ia-authoring method closure"
    status open
    milestone @milestone marketplace-published
    owner "Unassigned"
    start "2026-10-30"
    source "docs/roadmap.md"

@task drop-door-fallback
  meaning
    says "Once @inventarch/mcp-door ships ia_session, ia_catalogue and ia_method (the IA framework release after 3.4.1), move .mcp.json and the pins to it, drop the lanes' scripts/resolve.mjs fallback and make resolve.mjs a thin caller of the shared runtime's packet builder."
  work
    title "Drop the lanes' resolve.mjs fallback"
    status proposed
    milestone @milestone marketplace-published
    owner "Unassigned"
    start "2026-10-30"
    source "docs/roadmap.md"

@task codex-door-and-handlers
  meaning
    says "Give Codex the IA door and the kit handler hooks once qualified there: a Codex manifest entry or committed .codex/config.toml for the door, and a QUALIFIED_CODEX_HOOKS set for bootstrap.mjs and handlers.mjs."
  work
    title "Carry the door and kit handlers to Codex"
    status proposed
    milestone @milestone marketplace-published
    owner "Unassigned"
    start "2026-10-30"
    source "docs/roadmap.md"
